# Project conventions

Living rule for this repo. Add new sections here as conventions settle. Do not create a one-off rule for every topic unless it needs its own file and globs.

## API calls

Two maps in `src/lib/api/endpoints.ts`. Add a path to the map that owns it. Do not write a URL string at the call site.

| Map | Host | Caller |
|-----|------|--------|
| `endpoints` | This Next app (`/api/...`) | Browser and client components via `api()` |
| `backendEndpoints` | External API, prefixed with `API_URL` | Server route handlers via `callBackend()` |

`API_URL` empty means no external API. `callBackend()` returns `null`. Keep the local behavior. Do not invent a user or a successful upstream response.

### Browser

```ts
await api(endpoints.login, { method: "POST", body: values });
```

`api()` lives in `src/lib/api/client.ts`. That file is the only place that may `fetch` an `endpoints` path. Pass an `Endpoint` value, not a string.

### Server, talking to the external API

```ts
const upstream = await callBackend(backendEndpoints.login, { body: parsed.data });
if (upstream && !upstream.ok) {
  return upstreamFailure(upstream);
}
```

`callBackend()` and `backendUrl()` live in `src/lib/api/backend.ts`. That file is the only place that may join `API_URL` to a path.

### Adding an endpoint

1. Add the key to `endpoints`, `backendEndpoints`, or both.
2. Call it through `api()` or `callBackend()`.
3. Mark browser routes that must not refresh the session in `publicEndpoints`.

## Errors

Report unexpected failures with `reportError()` from `src/lib/report-error.ts`. Do not call a vendor SDK from a component. A project replaces the body of `reportError()` when it picks Sentry or another service.
